7. fsaverage5 surface and Destrieux atlas (FreeSurfer data, via Nilearn)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Files: frontend/public/brain/fsaverage5_pial_bilateral.bin
       frontend/public/brain/fsaverage5_parcellation.json

These files are modified versions of FreeSurfer data (the fsaverage5 pial
surfaces and the Destrieux aparc.a2009s parcellation), fetched with Nilearn
and converted by scripts/bake_fsaverage5.py. The backend also fetches the
Destrieux atlas through Nilearn at runtime for ROI aggregation.

All or portions of this licensed product (such portions are the "Software")
have been obtained under license from The General Hospital Corporation "MGH"
and are subject to the following terms and conditions: see the full FreeSurfer
Software License Agreement in frontend/public/brain/LICENSE-FreeSurfer.txt.

FreeSurfer: https://surfer.nmr.mgh.harvard.edu/
Please cite when using these assets:
  - Fischl B, Sereno MI, Tootell RBH, Dale AM. High-resolution intersubject
    averaging and a coordinate system for the cortical surface. Human Brain
    Mapping 8:272-284 (1999).
  - Destrieux C, Fischl B, Dale A, Halgren E. Automatic parcellation of human
    cortical gyri and sulci using standard anatomical nomenclature.
    NeuroImage 53(1):1-15 (2010).

Nilearn (https://nilearn.github.io/, BSD 3-Clause) is used to fetch and load
these datasets.

